# Server
PORT=3000

# Sentiment provider selection: inference | placeholder
# - inference (default): calls an OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint,
#   configured below. Works with Groq, local Ollama, or any other OpenAI-
#   compatible API -- swap providers by changing INFERENCE_BASE_URL/
#   INFERENCE_MODEL alone, no code changes needed. (Configurable this way at
#   Echory's explicit request, so they can point this backend at whichever
#   model works on their side.)
# - placeholder: rule-based, no LLM, no external dependency at all. Not the
#   default, but available as a manual override (set LLM_PROVIDER=placeholder)
#   if you want to see the API/UI working without an API key or Ollama.
LLM_PROVIDER=inference

# Used when LLM_PROVIDER=inference. Default below is Groq / qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# -- per Pascal's explicit answer (ticket 0018, 2026-09-04): don't assume GPU
# acceleration in a container, don't assume an install step on Echory's side,
# and default the inference endpoint to Groq. Get a free-tier key at
# https://console.groq.com/keys and paste it in below -- this project must
# not require paid API access to run.
INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
INFERENCE_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
INFERENCE_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key

# ---- The tradeoff behind that default, measured not assumed (tickets 0006, 0015, 0018) ----
#
#   Model              | Sentiment acc | Risk acc | Avg latency | % calls > 500ms
#   groq/qwen3.8-27b   |      93%       |   71%    |   378ms     |      14%
#   phi4-mini (local)  |      82%       |   75%    |   408ms     |       0%
#
# qwen3.8-27b beats phi4-mini on accuracy AND average latency, holdout-
# confirmed (not overfitting, unlike an earlier local candidate -- see
# docs/benchmark-results.md). Its real cost: a measured ~14% chance of any
# individual call exceeding the 500ms line, from Groq-side queue/network
# variance -- not something a prompt or code change fixes (directly tested:
# a shorter prompt doesn't help, prefill time isn't the bottleneck). Shipped
# as the default anyway, per Pascal's explicit answer that Echory's own
# infrastructure (no GPU passthrough assumed, no local-install step) rules
# out a local model as the *default* regardless of that model's latency
# safety margin -- and that documenting this tradeoff honestly is itself
# part of the task, not something to engineer away. Full numbers and the
# holdout methodology: docs/benchmark-results.md.

# ---- If you'd rather run the LLM locally instead (fully supported, just not default) ----
# Zero code changes, same InferenceProvider -- swap these three lines in:
#   INFERENCE_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#   INFERENCE_MODEL=phi4-mini
#   INFERENCE_API_KEY=
# `host.docker.internal`, not `localhost` -- inside the container, `localhost`
# means the container itself, not the host machine running Ollama. Docker
# Desktop resolves `host.docker.internal` to the host automatically on
# Windows/Mac. Requires `ollama pull phi4-mini` (~2.5GB, one-time) on the
# host first -- this is the one path in this project that needs something
# installed outside Docker, which is exactly why it's optional, not default
# (ticket 0017). `granite4.1:3b` is a safer-latency-margin local alternative
# (70% accuracy) -- switch via INFERENCE_MODEL alone.

# Opt-in escape hatch (ticket 0007), OFF by default. Only relevant if
# INFERENCE_MODEL above is switched to a local *reasoning* model -- Ollama's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint above cannot suppress "thinking" mode
# (think:false is silently ignored there), only Ollama's native /api/chat
# respects it (verified in ticket 0005). When set to true, the same
# InferenceProvider routes to native /api/chat with think:false instead of
# the default OpenAI-compatible call, derived from INFERENCE_BASE_URL by
# dropping the trailing /v1 -- no second base-URL var needed. Never set this
# for a cloud provider (Groq, etc.) -- it only makes sense for local Ollama.
# Not needed for phi4-mini/granite4.1:3b/qwen3.8-27b (all non-reasoning);
# verified working against a real local reasoning model (qwen3:8b) during
# ticket 0007's manual check even though no shipped model choice exercises
# it in production.
INFERENCE_DISABLE_THINKING=false

# Only used by scripts/llm-benchmark.ts (ticket 0006's local model quality
# benchmark) -- NOT required to run the actual backend. An external judge
# (rather than another local model) avoids competing with the models under
# test for the same GPU. DeepSeek's API is OpenAI-compatible.
JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
JUDGE_MODEL=deepseek-reasoner
JUDGE_API_KEY=your-deepseek-api-key
